Subject: [PATCH v10 0/3] usb: dwc3: support two connectors sharing one HS data
 bus

Changes since v9 (sashiko review of 2026-11-17, 2x High / 1x Medium / 2x
Low).  Every item was checked against the code and the binding; the two
High findings were real and are fixed, not argued away.

  [High] unbalanced mux_control_deselect() in __dwc3_set_mode()
    v9 called mux_control_deselect() unconditionally before selecting the
    new port.  On the initial mode request active_port is -1 and the mux
    has never been selected, so the deselect released a semaphore that
    was never taken.  Now only a mux that is actually selected is
    deselected, and a failed mux_control_select() records active_port =
    -1 instead of keeping the old index (which made the next request
    skip the select).  core.c in 3/3.

  [High] missing mux_control_deselect() on teardown in dwc3_drd_exit()
    devm_mux_control_get() only calls mux_control_put() on release; it
    does not restore the mux idle state.  v10 deselects the mux from
    dwc3_drd_exit() after cancel_work_sync(&dwc->drd_work), i.e. once no
    mode switch can select it again.  drd.c in 3/3.

  [Medium] unconditional hs-port on port@0 breaks non-mux DTs
    v9 required two endpoints and the address/size cells from every user
    of port@0, which rejected existing single-endpoint controllers.  The
    two endpoints and the opposite-mux-state rule are now required only
    when "mux-controls" is present; a single-connector controller keeps
    describing one plain "endpoint".  Verified with CHECK_DTBS=y on
    qcom/sm8250-mtp.dtb and qcom/sm8750-mtp.dtb (both rc=0, no
    diagnostics) and with the positive/negative dt-validate samples (see
    gates below).  binding in 1/3.

  [Low] hs-port allows omitting mux-state on one endpoint
    Both endpoints of the High Speed port now require "usb-role-switch"
    and "mux-state"; a tree that sets them on endpoint@0 only is
    rejected ('mux-state' is a required property on endpoint@1).
    binding in 1/3.

  [Low] commit message written as a v8-to-v9 changelog
    The binding commit now describes the new dual-connector description
    relative to the baseline tree; the inter-version changelog moved
    below the "---" separator.  binding in 1/3.

Note on 2/3: sashiko found no issues in the role-switch lookup patch; it
is unchanged from v9 apart from the series numbering.

The board-level DT change is still not part of this posting: port@0 gets
two endpoints and the Lenovo Legion Y700 Gen 4 describes the mux on GPIO
29 in the separate board DTS series, because that file is not upstream
yet.  No runtime testing is claimed for this version: the mux path has
not been exercised on hardware (this series was reviewed statically
only).

Gate results (base aebb727447 = v7.4-rc3, pristine worktree):
- git am: 3/3 applied cleanly.
- checkpatch --strict: 0 errors / 0 warnings / 0 checks on all three.
- make W=1 drivers/usb/dwc3/ drivers/usb/roles/ (arm64,
  CONFIG_MULTIPLEXER=y): rc=0, no warnings.
- make dt_binding_check DT_SCHEMA_FILES=.../snps,dwc3-common.yaml: rc=0.
- CHECK_DTBS=y qcom/sm8250-mtp.dtb qcom/sm8650-mtp.dtb qcom/sm8750-mtp.dtb
  (non-mux controllers): rc=0, no diagnostics.
- dt-validate positive sample (dual connector, mux-controls): PASS.
  Negative samples rejected: same mux state on both endpoints (oneOf),
  missing endpoint@1 (required), usb-role-switch/mux-state omitted on
  endpoint@1 (required), legacy v8 shape (unevaluated properties).

